---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About us" description="Learn about Back 2 School Africa Programme, its vision, mission, objectives and values as the nonprofit arm of Tutor Mentor Connect.">
  <section class="page-hero about-hero"><div class="wrap about-hero-grid">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">About us</span><h1>About Back 2 School Africa Programme</h1></div>
    <figure class="about-hero-photo"><img src="/images/joburg-library-learning.webp" width="634" height="615" alt="Children learning together with a tablet at a Johannesburg library" /><figcaption>Community learning at a Johannesburg library. Photo: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CHILDREN_USING_TABLETS_TO_PLAY_GAMES_AND_AND_READ_STORIES_AT_RABBI_RIDGE_LIBRARYJOBURG_SOUTH_AFRICA.jpg">JeffNyoka / Wikimedia Commons</a>, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>. Cropped and converted to WebP. This is not a Back 2 School Africa Programme photo.</figcaption></figure>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section" id="who-we-are"><div class="wrap two-col">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">Our organisation</span><h2>Who We Are</h2></div>
    <div class="prose"><p>Back 2 School Africa Programme is a nonprofit organisation dedicated to advancing education, youth development and community empowerment.</p><p>We work towards expanding access to educational information, learning initiatives, skills development and human rights education. Our approach recognises that young people need not only access to learning, but also guidance, resources and opportunities to progress.</p><p>Back 2 School Africa Programme is the nonprofit arm of Tutor Mentor Connect, a broader education technology and learning ecosystem. While Tutor Mentor Connect connects learners with educational services and learning opportunities, Back 2 School Africa Programme focuses on nonprofit initiatives and social impact.</p></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section wash" id="approach"><div class="wrap statement-grid">
    <article><span class="eyebrow">Looking ahead</span><h2>Our Vision</h2><p>A future in which every learner and young person has access to meaningful educational opportunities and the support needed to reach their potential.</p></article>
    <article><span class="eyebrow">Our work</span><h2>Our Mission</h2><p>To advance education and research, strengthen learning opportunities, promote volunteerism and contribute to social and community development through inclusive programmes and strategic partnerships.</p></article>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section about-objectives"><div class="wrap two-col">
    <div><span class="eyebrow light">Our work</span><h2>Our Objectives</h2></div>
    <div class="prose"><p>Our work is guided by our organisational constitution and objectives, including:</p><ul class="check-list"><li>Advancing education and research.</li><li>Supporting primary and secondary education.</li><li>Promoting volunteerism.</li><li>Contributing to social and community development.</li><li>Supporting activities aligned with international human rights and peace initiatives.</li></ul></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section wash"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">What guides us</span><h2 class="section-title">Our Values</h2><div class="values-grid">
    <article><h3>Opportunity</h3><p>Expanding access to education and pathways for growth.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Inclusion</h3><p>Respecting the dignity and potential of every learner.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Empowerment</h3><p>Equipping young people with knowledge, skills and information.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Collaboration</h3><p>Working with communities and partners towards shared goals.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Accountability</h3><p>Acting responsibly and communicating honestly about our work.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Community</h3><p>Supporting initiatives that respond to educational and social needs.</p></article>
  </div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
